Host tests of the patched tree link again: three upstream tests (tools/test_spu_raw_start.py, test_spu_raw_runcntl_stop.py,
test_spu_workload_masked.py) failed to link because files they compile reference hooks that live in files these tests do not
link (found by the Ratchet & Clank port, 2026-11-02). Spu pass 138.
- spu_fpmode.h: spu_fpmode_init_thread() (header-inline, the same rule as spu_host_fp_init in spu_drain.c, patch 1095); spu_raw.c
  and spu_workload.c call it, so a test that includes either alone no longer needs spu_drain.c. The SPURS kernels still call
  spu_host_fp_init.
- g_kz3_run_ctx_hook (patch 1081) is defined in spu_workload.c, next to the runner that calls it, instead of spu_channels.c.
- tools/test_spu_raw_runcntl_stop.py links the real runtime/diag/kz3_wait_acct.c (g_kz3_wacct, g_kz3_wtrace, kz3_wacct_*,
  patches 1032, 1085, 1135), like its other real runtime sources; test_spu_workload_masked.c, which replaces the coherency
  module with stand-ins, gets stand-ins for the striped lock-line API (spu_ll_mask, spu_ll_lock_mask, spu_ll_unlock_mask,
  patch 1056) next to the existing spu_lockline_lock/unlock one.

diff --git a/runtime/spu/spu_fpmode.h b/runtime/spu/spu_fpmode.h
